Another subtle thing: `ovsVsctl` prepends `--timeout=30` — but the ovs-vsctl `--timeout` option... yes, it takes seconds. OK.

**Now the `goOvs.Timeout` question.** Let me try to recall the exact API of digitalocean/go-openvswitch. I'm now fairly sure of the following from the library source (ovs/ovs.go):

```go
// Options contains various options to be used when creating a Client.
type Options struct {
	// Timeout is the timeout used for ovs commands.
	Timeout *time.Duration
}

// New returns a pointer to a new Client.
